   "text": "A woman left a promising legal career to become a dog walker, and says she now earns more money while working far less than she did before.\nLiz East worked as a paralegal in criminal defence for four years, trying to pursue her dream of becoming a criminal defence lawyer.\nHowever, as her career progressed Liz, 30, realised that she was becoming increasingly drained by the long gruelling hours, lea",
